Architecture Flow & Services:We need Amazon API Gateway $\to$ Amazon EventBridge (Custom Bus) $\to$ Amazon Data Firehose $\to$ Amazon S3 (with SQS as a Dead-Letter Queue).Required IAM Access & Permissions:API Gateway Role: Permission for events:PutEvents on the EventBridge bus.EventBridge Role: Permission for firehose:PutRecordBatch to the Firehose stream and sqs:SendMessage to the DLQ.Firehose Role: Permission for s3:PutObject (and multipart actions) on both the target landing path and the failure/error prefix in S3.   For a practical demonstration on setting up this direct pattern without writing extra compute code, see A Beginner's Tutorial with EventBridge & API Gateway.This video walks through connecting API Gateway directly to an EventBridge event bus to route incoming client events to downstream AWS targets.
